Vulkan: enable shaderStorageImageExtendedFormats when the device has it.

Blender-owned file; the hunk is enclosed in "UPBGE - Android" comments.
Not Android specific: a correct-usage fix that could go to Blender.

EEVEE declares storage images with extended formats (deferred light writes
RAYTRACE_RADIANCE_FORMAT = r11f_g11f_b10f), so its SPIR-V uses the
StorageImageExtendedFormats capability. GHOST never enabled the matching
device feature. Desktop drivers accept the pipeline anyway; the Mali driver
returns no pipeline for eevee_deferred_light_*, which is later bound as
VK_NULL_HANDLE and crashes in vkCmdBindPipeline.

Applies after 0003.

diff --git a/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_ContextVK.cc b/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_ContextVK.cc
index 60a0ec1..c8f5d92 100644
--- a/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_ContextVK.cc
+++ b/intern/ghost/intern/GHOST_ContextVK.cc
@@ -638,6 +638,13 @@ struct GHOST_InstanceVK {
     device_features.imageCubeArray = VK_TRUE;
     device_features.multiDrawIndirect = device.features.features.multiDrawIndirect;
     device_features.drawIndirectFirstInstance = VK_TRUE;
+    /* UPBGE - Android: EEVEE writes storage images with extended formats
+     * (r11f_g11f_b10f, rg16f, ...), so its SPIR-V declares the
+     * StorageImageExtendedFormats capability, which requires this feature.
+     * Desktop drivers tolerate it missing; Mali refuses to build the pipeline. */
+    device_features.shaderStorageImageExtendedFormats =
+        device.features.features.shaderStorageImageExtendedFormats;
+    /* UPBGE - Android */
     device_features.samplerAnisotropy = device.features.features.samplerAnisotropy;
     device_features.wideLines = device.features.features.wideLines;
 
